# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  DENY ALL — database/ is application code, never web content.
#
#  Layer 3 of the protection described in the project-root .htaccess, and the only
#  layer that does not depend on any other file. It exists because the root
#  .htaccess is what an operator edits when the site returns 403 for every URL —
#  which is exactly what happened here — and emptying that file must not silently
#  publish the source tree, the .env, the migrations and the logs.
#
#  Correct hosting makes this redundant: with DocumentRoot at ./public, nothing
#  outside public/ is reachable at all and this file is never even read. It is
#  here for the deployment where that is not true.
#
#  mod_authz_core (Apache 2.4 / LiteSpeed) with a 2.2 fallback, and nothing else.
#  A directive the server does not understand in .htaccess is a 500 for the whole
#  site, and this file is copied into eleven directories.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
  Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
  Order allow,deny
  Deny from all
</IfModule>
